The triangle inequality theorem states that the sum of the lengths of any two sides of a triangle must be greater than the length of the remaining side. Let's denote the third side of the triangle as \( x \).

Given sides are 12 and 7, we have:
1. \( 12 + 7 > x \) which simplifies to \( 19 > x \) or \( x < 19 \)
