\]

Now, find the vertical velocity at \(t = 1.92\):
\[
\frac{dy}{dt} = 4.2 - 9.8(1.92) \approx 4.2 - 18.816 \approx -14.616 \, \text{m/s}
\]

The slope of the path is:
\[
\text{slope} = \frac{\frac{dy}{dt}}{\frac{dx}{dt}} = \frac{-14.616}{1.4} \approx -10.44
\]

The angle \(\theta\) is given by:
\[
\tan(\theta) = \left| \frac{\frac{dy}{dt}}{\frac{dx}{dt}} \right| = 10.44
\]

So,
\[
\theta = \tan^{-1}(10.44) \approx 1.475 \, \text{radians}
\]

