   The base current \( I_B \) can be found using the voltage divider rule for the base biasing network:
   \[
   I_B = \frac{V_{CC} \cdot R_2}{R_1 + R_2 + (\beta + 1) \cdot R_E}
   \]
   Given:
   - \( V_{CC} = 18 \, \text{V} \)
   - \( R_1 = 33 \, \text{k}\Omega \)
