 To find the sum of the elements that are unique to set A and set B (excluding the intersection), we need to add the unique elements of each set.

- The unique elements of set A are \( n(A) - n(A \cap B) = 140 - 60 = 80 \).
- The unique elements of set B are \( n(B) - n(A \cap B) = 120 - 60 = 60 \).

Adding these unique elements together:
\[ 80 + 60 = 140 \]

Thus, the sum of the elements that are unique to set A and set B (excluding the intersection) is 140.

Answer: A
