     \]
   - At \( x = 8 \):
     \[
     \frac{dy}{dx} = \frac{1}{8 \ln(2)}
     \]
   Since \( 6 < 8 \), it follows that \( \frac{1}{6 \ln(2)} > \frac{1}{8 \ln(2)} \).

Therefore, the derivative of \( y \) at \( x = 6 \) is larger than the derivative at \( x = 8 \).

