   - The ship sails from point A to point B in 30 minutes (0.5 hours) at a speed of 40.0 nautical miles per hour.
   - Distance = Speed × Time
   - Distance \( AB = 40.0 \, \text{nautical miles per hour} \times 0.5 \, \text{hours} = 20 \, \text{nautical miles} \)

2. **Determine the coordinates of points A and B:**
   - Let's assume point A is at the origin (0, 0).
