     A_{\text{original}} = 2 \times 216 = 432 \text{ square units}
     \]

2. **Calculate the surface area of the cut-out section:**
   - The cut-out section is a rectangular prism with dimensions 5 units (length), 3 units (width), and 6 units (height).
   - The surface area \( A_{\text{cut-out}} \) of the cut-out section is given by:
     \[
     A_{\text{cut-out}} = 2(lw + lh + wh)
     \]
