     \[
     A_{\text{cut-out}} = 2(5 \times 3 + 5 \times 6 + 3 \times 6)
     \]
     \[
     A_{\text{cut-out}} = 2(15 + 30 + 18)
     \]
     \[
     A_{\text{cut-out}} = 2 \times 63 = 126 \text{ square units}
     \]

3. **Calculate the new surface area of the block after the cut-out:**
   - The new surface area \( A_{\text{new}} \) is the original surface area minus the surface area of the cut-out section:
     \[
     A_{\text{new}} = A_{\text{original}} - A_{\text{cut-out}}
