1. **Find the side length of the square:**
   - The perimeter of the square is given as \(48 \text{ cm}\).
   - The formula for the perimeter of a square is \(4 \times \text{side length}\).
   - Let \(s\) be the side length of the square.
   - Therefore, \(4s = 48\).
   - Solving for \(s\), we get \(s = \frac{48}{4} = 12 \text{ cm}\).

2. **Determine the dimensions of the rectangle:**
   - When the square is cut into two equal pieces along one of its sides, each piece will have dimensions \(12 \text{ cm} \times 6 \text{ cm}\) (since the height is halved).
