3. **Calculate the perimeter of the rectangle:**
   - The formula for the perimeter of a rectangle is \(2 \times (\text{length} + \text{width})\).
   - Here, the length is \(12 \text{ cm}\) and the width is \(12 \text{ cm}\).
   - Therefore, the perimeter is \(2 \times (12 + 12) = 2 \times 24 = 48 \text{ cm}\).

Thus, the perimeter of the rectangle is \(48 \text{ cm}\).

