\[ 40 - b = 42 \]
\[ -b = 2 \]
\[ b = -2 \] (not a valid digit)

2. If \( a = 5 \):
\[ 10(5) - b = 42 \]
\[ 50 - b = 42 \]
\[ -b = -8 \]
\[ b = 8 \] (valid digit)

So, \( a = 5 \) and \( b = 8 \).

The sum of the two painted digits is:
\[ a + b = 5 + 8 = 13 \]

