Question: A big cube is made up of 64 small cubes. Exactly one of these cubes is grey (see diagram). Two cubes are neighbours if they share a common face. On day one the grey cube colours all its neighbouring cubes grey. On day two all grey cubes again colour all their neighbouring cubes grey. How many of the 64 little cubes are grey at the end of the second day?
