### Step-by-Step Solution:

1. **Identify the surface areas of the cuboids formed by placing two bricks side by side:**
   - When placed side by side along the length, the surface area is \( 72 \, \text{cm}^2 \).
   - When placed side by side along the width, the surface area is \( 96 \, \text{cm}^2 \).
   - When placed side by side along the height, the surface area is \( 102 \, \text{cm}^2 \).

2. **Express the surface areas of the cuboids in terms of the brick dimensions:**
   - For the cuboid formed by placing the bricks along the length:
     \[
