   - For an \(n \times n\) pattern, the number of matchsticks used can be calculated as follows:
     - Each row of \(n\) squares requires \(2n\) matchsticks (top and bottom).
     - There are \(n\) rows, so the total number of matchsticks for the horizontal lines is \(2n \times n = 2n^2\).
     - Similarly, each column of \(n\) squares requires \(2n\) matchsticks (left and right).
