   The area of the large square is given as \(81 \text{ cm}^2\). Since the area of a square is the side length squared, we can find the side length of the large square:
   \[
   \text{Side length of the large square} = \sqrt{81} = 9 \text{ cm}
   \]

2. **Area of the square formed by the diagonals of the rectangles:**
   The area of the square formed by the diagonals of the rectangles is given as \(64 \text{ cm}^2\). Similarly, we can find the side length of this square:
   \[
   \text{Side length of the square formed by the diagonals} = \sqrt{64} = 8 \text{ cm}
   \]

