   The side length of the square formed by the diagonals of the rectangles is equal to the diagonal of one of the rectangles. The diagonal of a rectangle with side lengths \(a\) and \(b\) is given by:
   \[
   \text{Diagonal} = \sqrt{a^2 + b^2}
   \]
