   - The sum of the angles in any triangle is \(180^\circ\).
   - Therefore, \(\angle PQR + \angle PRQ + \angle QPR = 180^\circ\).
   - Let \(\angle PQR = \angle PRQ = x\).
   - So, \(x + x + 20^\circ = 180^\circ\).
