 To determine the number of rings used in the chain, we need to calculate the length of one ring and then divide the total length of the chain by the length of one ring.

1. **Calculate the circumference of the outer circle:**
   The external radius \( R \) is 3 cm.
   \[
   \text{Circumference of the outer circle} = 2 \pi R = 2 \pi \times 3 = 6 \pi \text{ cm}
   \]

2. **Calculate the circumference of the inner circle:**
   The internal radius \( r \) is 2 cm.
   \[
   \text{Circumference of the inner circle} = 2 \pi r = 2 \pi \times 2 = 4 \pi \text{ cm}
   \]

3. **Calculate the length of one ring:**
   The length of one ring is the difference between the outer and inner circumferences.
   \[
   \text{Length of one ring} = 6 \pi - 4 \pi = 2 \pi \text{ cm}
   \]

4. **Convert the total length of the chain to centimeters:**
   The total length of the chain is 1.7 meters.
   \[
   1.7 \text{ m} = 1.7 \times 100 = 170 \text{ cm}
   \]

5. **Calculate the number of rings:**
   Divide the total length of the chain by the length of one ring.
   \[
