   - The total length of the chain is 1.7 meters.
   - Convert meters to centimeters:
     \[
     1.7 \text{ m} = 1.7 \times 100 \text{ cm} = 170 \text{ cm}
     \]

3. **Calculate the number of rings:**
   - The number of rings \( N \) is the total length of the chain divided by the circumference of one ring:
     \[
     N = \frac{\text{Total length}}{\text{Circumference of one ring}} = \frac{170 \text{ cm}}{5 \pi \text{ cm}}
     \]
