\hline
\end{array}
\]

We know that the product in the bottom right cell is 77. This cell is the product of \( (y+1) \) and \( x \):

\[
(y+1)x = 77
\]

We need to find the integer values of \( y \) and \( x \) that satisfy this equation, with \( x \) being greater than \( y \).

