\[ A_{\text{total}} = A_{\text{triangle}} + A_{\text{circle}} - A_{\text{intersection}} \]
\[ A_{\text{total}} = 0.85 \times A_{\text{total}} + A_{\text{circle}} - 0.45 \times A_{\text{total}} \]
\[ A_{\text{total}} = 0.40 \times A_{\text{total}} + A_{\text{circle}} \]
\[ A_{\text{circle}} = 0.60 \times A_{\text{total}} \]

Now, we can find \(A_{\text{circle outside triangle}}\):
\[ A_{\text{circle outside triangle}} = A_{\text{circle}} - A_{\text{intersection}} \]
\[ A_{\text{circle outside triangle}} = 0.60 \times A_{\text{total}} - 0.45 \times A_{\text{total}} \]
\[ A_{\text{circle outside triangle}} = 0.15 \times A_{\text{total}} \]

The percentage of the circle that lies outside the triangle is:
\[ \frac{A_{\text{circle outside triangle}}}{A_{\text{circle}}} \times 100\% \]
\[ \frac{0.15 \times A_{\text{total}}}{0.60 \times A_{\text{total}}} \times 100\% \]
\[ \frac{0.15}{0.60} \times 100\% \]
\[ 0.25 \times 100\% \]
\[ 25\% \]

Therefore, the percentage of the circle that lies outside the triangle is \(\boxed{25\%}\). The correct option is \(\boxed{B}\).
