   The side length of the cube is \(8\) feet. The diagonal \(d\) of a cube with side length \(s\) can be calculated using the formula:
   \[
   d = s\sqrt{3}
   \]
   Substituting \(s = 8\):
   \[
   d = 8\sqrt{3}
   \]

2. **Determine the submerged height of the cube:**
   Since the diagonal of the cube is vertical and the barrel has a height of \(10\) feet, the entire cube will be submerged because \(8\sqrt{3} \approx 13.856\) feet, which is greater than \(10\) feet. Therefore, the entire volume of the cube will displace water.

